From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] platform: arm64: huawei-gaokun-ec: 挂起期间关掉EC中断

EC进入待机（EC_STANDBY_ENTER）以后，中断处理函数读不了EC，所以碰到
ec->suspended就直接返回。可这个中断是电平触发的：事件没读走，线一直拉着，
处理函数一返回，中断马上又进来。从休眠醒来时，EC往往有事件等着报，于是在EC
恢复之前，这个线程要空转一到三秒、上万次（本机一次开机里7次休眠，累计约9万次）。

改为在suspend里先disable_irq()（它会等正在运行的处理函数结束），resume里EC
退出待机以后再enable_irq()。期间来的事件留在EC里，恢复后照常读出，不会丢。
EC中断作为唤醒源时照样能唤醒：PDC带IRQCHIP_ENABLE_WAKEUP_ON_SUSPEND，中断
核心挂起时会重新打开被关掉的唤醒中断。处理函数里的ec->suspended检查随之去掉。
---
 drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c | 20 +++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c b/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
index 4c74447..06b9222 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/arm64/huawei-gaokun-ec.c
@@ -629,9 +629,22 @@ static int gaokun_ec_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	if (ec->suspended)
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * The handler cannot read the EC in standby, and the IRQ is level
+	 * triggered: it would fire again as soon as the handler returned.
+	 * Keep it disabled until resume. An event raised meanwhile keeps the
+	 * line asserted, and the handler reads it once resume enables the
+	 * IRQ again. As a wakeup IRQ it still wakes the system: the PDC has
+	 * the irq core enable disabled wakeup IRQs for suspend
+	 * (IRQCHIP_ENABLE_WAKEUP_ON_SUSPEND).
+	 */
+	disable_irq(ec->client->irq);
+
 	ret = gaokun_ec_write(ec, ec_req);
-	if (ret)
+	if (ret) {
+		enable_irq(ec->client->irq);
 		return ret;
+	}
 
 	msleep(100);
 	gpiod_set_value(ec->enable_gpio, 0);
@@ -671,6 +684,7 @@ static int gaokun_ec_resume(struct device *dev)
 	ec->lid_opened = true;
 
 	ec->suspended = false;
+	enable_irq(ec->client->irq);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -735,10 +749,6 @@ static irqreturn_t gaokun_ec_irq_handler(int irq, void *data)
 	u8 status, id;
 	int ret;
 
-	/* EC IO here before resume will fail at the first time, so ignore it */
-	if (ec->suspended)
-		return IRQ_HANDLED;
-
 	ret = gaokun_ec_read_byte(ec, ec_req, &id);
 	if (ret)
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
